re short-lived credentials'), ('A05', 'No way to trace a suspicious action to its team, o')]\n   FAIL B04.3 app/identity.py:97 :: Broker serves cached access tokens until expiry with no revocation check. The repo states no revocation time limit. Access-token lifetime comes from the STS (identity.py:115). No introspection, deny list or CAEP push appears. Open runs continue because killswitch is checked only at start (loop.py:127, main.py:159).\n-- E09 Recursive shutdown | also []\n   REQ: Run a drill across a parent, nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.\n   NOTCOVERED: [('R11', 'Agent able to disable or delay its own stop'), ('B04', \"No way to cut off the agent's access without cutti\"), ('E12', 'No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent ty'), ('E08', 'Sub-agent given powers beyond its task')]\n   FAIL E09.2 app/identity.py:97 :: Stop revokes nothing: no revoke or lease release exists. Cached backend tokens stay valid until their own expiry (set by the STS, not bounded here) and descendants keep using them.\n######### app/killswitch.py 19 ['A05', 'E03']\nCODE: AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = $1)\n-- A05 Operational lookup | also []\n   REQ: Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\n   NOTCOVERED: [('R11', \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool stream\"), ('E12', 'No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent ty'), ('A02', 'Action records missing any of the six identity fie')]\n   FAIL A05.3 app/killswitch.py:19 :: Halt scopes are fleet or one tenant (migrations/001_init.sql:9